   "etymology": "Inherited from Common Albanian *əzbréz (with final devoicing to -s), from Proto-Albanian *əzbredᶻə, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *ezbrédyV, with synocope from older *ezbrédiyV, with i-umlaut from older PPA *ezbrádiyV (\"to move out, go away\"). The word may be dissected as *ez-brádiyV, with the *ez- prefix being inherited from Proto-Indo-European *eǵʰs (“out”), and the base *brádiyV (\"to move, roam\") being inherited from Proto-Indo-European *bʰrodʰéye/o- (“to wade”), from Proto-Indo-European *bʰredʰ- (“to wade”).",
